TILE ENGINE RETRO — RESURRECTION PLAN (2026-07-26)

Goal: back from the graveyard, nice demo for Luis in a few weeks.

== 1. RESURRECTION (make it build and run again) ==

[x] Load bg0.gfx into bg[0] (was loading bg1.gfx twice)
[x] Fix hardcoded /home/daniel/... music path (load test.xm relative to cwd,
    same as the .gfx files)
[x] NULL-check every fopen; missing assets log an error instead of segfaulting
[x] Remove unused audiofile handle (fopen("airwolf2.mod") / fclose(NULL) crash)
[x] Root + core Makefiles work on modern macOS (arm64, .dylib); drop dead
    -arch i386/x86_64 universal flags; make clean uses rm -f
[x] libxmp optional behind HAVE_XMP (auto-detected via pkg-config, override
    with make HAVE_XMP=0/1); core builds silent without it
[x] Fix delete_fsp/delete_hsp underflow (OOB read/infinite loop when deleting
    the last sprite)
[x] add_player handles add_fsp failure instead of using 32 as a sprite id
[x] add_projectile increments projectile_count
[x] player.score uint16_t -> uint32_t (default hi-scores exceed 65535)
[x] Normalize diagonal speed (DIA_SPD 12 -> 8, ~= 12/sqrt(2))
[x] Delete vestigial libretro-example skeleton: x_coord/y_coord fake
    serialization, retro_load_game_special magic numbers

== 2. ENGINE CORRECTNESS & COMPLETENESS ==

[x] SoA it is: game2.h completed and wired in, game.h deleted
    (the uint8_t<256 infinite loop died with the port)
[x] OAM transforms, all of them: h-flip + rotate +/-90 via pre-computed
    tileset variants (memory), v-flip + double-size at render time (cpu);
    rotation+h_flip+v_flip composes to -90
[x] Collisions: AABB on the packed dimensions words (projectiles vs
    enemies, players vs enemies) — no wraparound handling yet
[x] Free lists replace the active_number high-water mark (O(1) alloc,
    double-free guard)
[x] Readme reconciled with code: 4bpp everywhere (hsp now 8 palettes x 16
    colors, dead 3bpp masks deleted), 512x512 layers kept, actual GFX byte
    format documented, real render order (BG1, BG0, SP0, SP1) documented
[x] Save states: versioned manifest of memcpy'd blocks (~15 KB), verified
    byte-identical on a serialize/restore/replay round trip

== 3. RENDERER == (all done — verified pixel-identical by frame CRCs,
                    2.8x faster: 0.154 -> 0.055 ms/frame at -O3)

[x] Span rendering: one tilemap lookup per tile-aligned span, no per-pixel
    div/mod (render_bg_scanline)
[x] The 3x-duplicated BG1 sampling collapsed into render_bg_scanline,
    shared by both layers via a base/overlay flag
[x] 8-pixel uint32_t fetch consumed with a rolling shift (bg) / cached
    group (sprites)
[x] Sprites clipped once per sprite: at most two visible x spans
    (wraparound), no per-pixel bounds checks
[x] Background cache: bg layers composed into bg_cache, recomposed only
    when scroll/animation/palettes change (bg_cache_dirty), memcpy'd per
    frame with sprites drawn on top
[x] Fade in/out via palette darkening: set_fade(0..32) recomputes live
    palettes from bases; boot does a 64-frame fade-in from black
[x] Vertical flip, rotation (see OAM transforms above)

== 4. TOOLING == (gfxtool replaces bmptogfx; legacy outputs verified
                   byte-identical before the switch)

[x] Manifest-driven conversion (assets/*.mfst): type + tileset + palette
    lines with alpha= flags replace positional args, the 4x4-BMP palette
    heuristic, and .pal.clr sidecars
[x] PNG input and output via vendored stb_image / stb_image_write;
    indexed BMPs keep their exact pixel indices via qdbmp
[x] Reverse direction: gfxtool dump renders any .gfx as a contact sheet
[x] Deduplicate identical tiles: gfxtool import-scene turns a 512x512
    scene image into a tileset + 32x32 .map (98% saved on the test scene);
    mirrored-tile dedup waits for background flip support in the renderer
[x] Tilemap pipeline: MAP file format + read_map_data() replace the
    hand-poked pattern for authored scenes (Tiled .tmx superseded by
    scene images and generated maps; revisit if a real level editor lands)
[x] Validation everywhere: unknown colors (with pixel position), bad
    dimensions, tile overflow, unknown directives — all fail loudly

== 5. STRUCTURE & LONGEVITY == (all done; refactor verified pixel-identical
                                 by frame CRCs)

[x] Engine split into gfx_engine.h (interface) + gfx_engine.c (library);
    the core links two objects now
[x] All engine state in an explicit gfx_context; the engine has no globals
    of its own (the app owns one instance, GFX, in game2.h)
[x] test/units.c, run by make test: 67 checks over bit-pack accessors,
    AABB, color math, tile packing, GFX/MAP parser round trips, transform
    variant involutions, the OAM free list
[x] PNG-out harness: HARNESS_DUMP=<prefix> make the harness write frames
    as PNGs — the engine runs and screenshots with no frontend at all
[x] Timeline system (game2.h tl_event): scripted "at frame N do X" with
    looping waves, replacing the hard-coded spawner cadence-exactly
[x] Audio proper: 44.1 kHz stereo via audio_batch_cb, four synthesized
    SFX voices (laser, boom, plop, blip) mixed over the libxmp music
[x] -Wall -Wextra -pedantic clean; .clang-format added (apply to files as
    you touch them); README.md with build/run + screenshots (a GIF wants
    a capture tool — PNGs for now)

== DEMO TARGET (Readme "Roadmap to 0.1", the unfinished half) ==

[x] Collisions
[ ] Sprites for ships, explosions and bullets (dedicated art)
[x] Audio for bullets and hits (synthesized; sampled SFX later maybe)
[ ] One level and boss (the timeline system is the tool for this)

== SCENES ==

1 Asteroid Run (shmup, the original), 2 Crystal Cavern (shmup, generated
art), 3 Koi Pond (top-down zen pond: rotation as fish headings, scanline
sine warp as refraction, semitransparent ripples/light, palette-rotated
caustics). Scene kinds live in core/libretro-core.c scene_defs.
